{
  "note": [
    "Reactor Control's fabric (DR-106, the mech wing), cut from the one Kalamontee layout in scripts/fabric-kalamontee.mjs -- regenerate from there, do not hand-edit. 8 x 3.6 x 8, the eye at the middle. The game: \"many dials and gauges for controlling a massive planetary power reactor which, according to a diagram on the wall, must be buried far below this very complex. The exit is to the west. To the east is a metal door, and next to it, a button. A dark stairway winds downward\" (compone.zil 1451-1454).",
    "Consoles of dials and gauges along the south wall and under the diagram on the north wall's west half; gauge panels either side of the west door and on the east wall south of the elevator door. West, the 1.2 x 2.25 door onto the Mech Corridor (its bare west wall). East, 0.5 m south of the eye, the reactor elevator's 2 x 2.5 metal doors, framed, the button beside them on the north: REACTOR-ELEVATOR-DOOR, shut (a pair of leaves) or open onto the lit car; the one switch here. North, 1.3 m east of the middle, a 1.4 x 2.3 doorway onto the stair shaft: dark, the post and the top steps dropping away inside a 0.3 m sill."
